    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Here we present the current status of the Structural Geology Knowledge Base and the design shift resulting from the addition of the ontology structure. Most of the logical module is completed; this provides a full-line of service starting with the identification of deformation mechanisms, continuing with the determination of the geometry and distribution of fractures, and then ending with the estimation of petrophysical properties for the resulted structural elements. The ontology is domain- specific, aiming to provide explanations to logical module as well to serve other general uses such as geological knowledge sharing.",
